<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#08090b"><title>Request account deletion · PixelWalls</title><meta name="description" content="How to contact PixelWalls support to request deletion of your account and related data."><link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/pixelwalls-pages.css"></head><body class="pw-page"><a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="pw-header"><div class="pw-nav"><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="SoftPixels home"><span class="pixel-mark" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>softpixels<span class="brand-dot">.</span></a><nav aria-label="PixelWalls pages"><a href="/pixelwalls/privacy-policy/">Privacy</a><a href="/pixelwalls/terms/">Terms</a><a href="/pixelwalls/help-support/">Help &amp; support</a></nav></div></header><main id="main" class="pw-main"><a class="pw-back" href="/">← SoftPixels</a><p class="eyebrow">PIXELWALLS · INFORMATION</p><h1>Request account deletion</h1><p>You can request deletion of your PixelWalls account by emailing <a href="mailto:sachinsingh200842@gmail.com?subject=PixelWalls%20account%20deletion">sachinsingh200842@gmail.com</a> from the email address linked to your Google sign-in. Use the subject <strong>PixelWalls account deletion</strong>.</p><h2>What to include</h2><ul><li>The email address associated with the PixelWalls account.</li><li>A short request to delete the account.</li><li>Optional context that helps us identify the request.</li></ul><p>Do not include your password, date of birth, or other sensitive details. We may ask for reasonable verification to confirm you control the account before acting.</p><h2>What the request covers</h2><p>We will review deletion of your Firebase Authentication account and associated PixelWalls profile data, such as synced favorites and notification token, where applicable. Wallpapers you downloaded or favorites stored only on your device can be removed by clearing PixelWalls app data or uninstalling the app. Public wallpaper catalog content is not personal account data. Some records may need to be retained where required or permitted by law or for security and dispute handling.</p><h2>Timing and confirmation</h2><p>Support will review the request and respond by email. We do not provide an automated deletion form or promise a fixed completion time here. Signing out or uninstalling the app does not itself delete server-side account data.</p><p>Read the <a href="/pixelwalls/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> or visit <a href="/pixelwalls/help-support/">Help &amp; Support</a>.</p></main><footer class="pw-footer"><a href="/">SoftPixels home</a><span>© 2026 PixelWalls · SoftPixels</span><a href="mailto:sachinsingh200842@gmail.com">Contact</a></footer></body></html>
